      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the product of \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\), we need to multiply the two fractions together. The general rule for multiplying fractions is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a}{b} \\times \\frac{c}{d} = \\frac{a \\times c}{b \\times d}\n\\]\n\nHere, \\(a = 1\\), \\(b = 5\\), \\(c = 3\\), and \\(d = 7\\). Applying the rule, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{5} \\times \\frac{3}{7} = \\frac{1 \\times 3}{5 \\times 7} = \\frac{3}{35}\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{3}{35}}\\).",
